8#,#8 Major#,#Physics#,#Bachelor of Science in Physics (Focused Option)
This option—which includes three terms of quantum mechanics, 36 units of laboratory experience, and a thesis—is ideal preparation for a career in physics.

An important component of this option is the thesis, which is a physics research project carried out under the guidance of a faculty member. Many thesis projects grow naturally out of UROP projects. Students should have some idea of a thesis topic by the middle of the junior year. A thesis proposal must be submitted before registering for thesis units and no later than Add Date of the fall term of the senior year.

required_subjects

restricted_electives

cim


required_subjects, "Required Subjects" := (18.03/18.032), 8.03, 8.033, 8.04, 8.044, 8.05, 8.06, 8.13, 8.14, 8.223, 8.THU

%% Math subject beyond 18.03: Any Course 18 subject beyond intro level
%% 18.04, 18.075, and 18.06 are noted as "particularly popular with physics majors"
%% Including all undergraduate Course 18 subjects that are beyond 18.03
math_beyond_1803, "Math Subject Beyond 18.03" := 18.04/18.05/18.06/18.075/18.C06/18.100A/18.100B/18.100P/18.100Q/18.101/18.102/18.103/18.104/18.112/18.152/18.200/18.200A/18.204/18.211/18.212/18.300/18.303/18.330/18.352/18.353/18.354/18.384/18.400/18.404/18.410/18.413/18.424/18.434/18.453/18.504/18.510/18.600/18.604/18.642/18.650/18.700/18.701/18.702/18.703/18.704/18.721/18.781/18.782/18.783/18.784/18.821/18.900/18.901/18.904/18.950/18.952/18.994{>=1}

%% Additional physics subject: Course 8 subjects not already required and not excluded
%% Excluded per catalog: 8.20 (Introduction to Special Relativity), 8.282 (Introduction to Astronomy)
%% Also excluded: GIRs (8.01/8.02 series), required subjects, alternate versions (8.041, 8.051)
%% Included: All undergraduate Course 8 subjects >= 9 units not otherwise excluded
additional_physics, "Additional Physics Subject" := 8.07/8.08/8.09/8.16/8.21/8.224/8.225/8.226/8.231/8.241/8.251/8.276/8.284/8.286/8.287/8.290/8.292{>=1}

%% At least one of 8.07, 8.08, or 8.09 required
theory_sequence, "Theory Sequence Subject" := 8.07/8.08/8.09{>=1}

restricted_electives, "Restricted Electives" := math_beyond_1803, additional_physics, theory_sequence

%% CI-M requirement: students must select 2 from this list
%% Per MIT catalog: 8.06, 8.13, 8.14, 8.226, 12.410[J], STS.042[J]
%% Note: 8.13 and 8.14 are also required subjects, so they double-count
cim, "Communication-Intensive Subjects" := 8.06/8.13/8.14/8.226/12.410/STS.042{>=2}
